plugin-qualify (0.16.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * version 0.16.0
  * Declare the schema-floor refusal code and the id-hash prefix for
    descriptors.py#142
  * commit-message-check: the self-test strings name no private pointer
  * debian: python3-lilv is a dependency on every suite that carries it (#168)
  * tools: install-roundtrip.sh, the after-install scan on a clean image
    (#168)
  * sync: a plugin that is gone leaves no record, descriptor or pin behind
    (#168)
  * sync tests: the path unit's standard folders are watched; the settings
    file adds the rest (#168)
  * packaging: the install check allows the trigger's scan, and refuses one
    that qualified a plugin (#168)
  * packaging: the sync service carries its own limits (#168)
  * packaging: the path unit names the standard folders; the settings file
    adds the rest (#168)
  * packaging: a package transaction in a plugin folder scans once (#168)
  * CI: the commit-message check is the commit-message-check action

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:58:51 +0000
